cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GameInferfarm in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GameInferfarm: a game-agnostic C++ inference farm for self-play, RL evaluation and evolutionary search"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: SkYContact
repository-code: "https://github.com/SkYContact/GameInferfarm"
url: "https://github.com/SkYContact/GameInferfarm"
abstract: >-
  GameInferfarm turns "run a huge number of homogeneous games concurrently,
  batch every neural-net decision" into a game-agnostic library: a fiber
  scheduler eliminates per-decision thread wakeups, zero-copy slot banks with
  per-bank CUDA Graphs amortize the small-batch GPU ticket tax, multi-device
  groups split one GPU into parallel fill pipelines (NVIDIA CUDA/TensorRT and
  AMD DirectML, including mixed-vendor multi-GPU), and per-generation
  population routing serves evolutionary workloads. Measured 116x over a naive
  python loop on the public Gomoku benchmark; bitwise determinism gates
  (G1-G9) enforced in CI. MIT license.
keywords:
  - self-play
  - batched inference
  - reinforcement-learning
  - evolutionary-computation
  - game-ai
  - high-throughput
  - CUDA-Graph
  - DirectML
license: MIT
